# Lesson 3, new exercise: count losers in a trump contract, then ruff the extra ones in dummy.
title: Too many losers? Use dummy's trumps
id: L03-02
type: exercise
lesson: 3
concepts: 3.3
student: S
board: 34
dealer: E
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  K53    Q842   A      Q8652
  E  QJT9   T9     QJ73   743
  S  A84    AKJ76  K652   9
  W  762    53     T984   AKJT

auction:
  E Pass
  S 1H     = 13+ points, at least four hearts
  W Pass
  N 3H     = 4+ hearts, 12-13 points: game forcing
  E Pass
  S 4H     = Game
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  You opened 1♥ and partner jumped to 3♥, showing four hearts and 12-13
  points, so you bid game. You are declarer, because you bid hearts first,
  and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  trumps out: 4
  losers: 2
  spades: 1 = The third spade. Nothing to be done about it.
  hearts: 0 = Solid.
  diamonds: 0 = Two small ones after the ace and king, but dummy can ruff both.
  clubs: 1 = The ace.
  remind: You can afford three losers in 4♥. Count the obvious losers suit by suit in your own hand: spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs.
  remind: How could dummy's trumps help with the diamonds?
play:
  1   W CA  N C2  E C3  S C9
      note: West leads the ace of clubs. That's one of your losers gone already.
  2   W H5  N H2  E H9  S HJ
  3   S HK  W H3  N H4  E HT
      note: The plan: draw trumps, then ruff two diamonds in dummy. One more round of trumps, and both opponents follow.
  4   S D2  W D4  N DA  E D3
      note: Trumps are drawn, and dummy still has two left. Start on diamonds with dummy's ace.
  5   N S3  E S9  S SA  W S2
      note: Back to your hand with the ♠A.
  6   S DK  W D8  N C5  E D7
      note: Your ♦K wins. Dummy doesn't ruff your own winner: throw a club.
  7   S D5  W D9  N H8*  E DJ
      note: Now ruff a losing diamond with a small trump.
      H8 key: Dummy has no diamonds left, so it can ruff your loser.
      H8 not *: Did you count your losers? Dummy has no diamonds, so it can trump this one.
  8   N C6  E C4  S H6  W CT
      note: Ruff a club to get back to your hand.
  9   S D6  W DT  N HQ*  E DQ
      note: And ruff your last diamond loser.
      HQ key: Ruff your last diamond loser with dummy's last trump.
      HQ not *: Did you count your losers? Dummy can still ruff this diamond.
  10  N SK  E ST  S S4  W S6
      note: Cash the ♠K.
  11  N S5  E SJ  S S8  W S7
      note: The third spade is a loser you can't avoid.
  12  E SQ  S H7  W CJ  N C8
  13  S HA  W CK  N CQ  E C7
      note: 11 tricks: 4♥ made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  The plan: you counted four losers, one spade, two diamonds and one club,
  one too many for 4♥. Dummy's short diamonds and spare trumps took care of
  the diamonds: each ruff turned a loser into a winner.
